# SRG-APP-000514-AU-002890  -  CAT I
# The Central Log Server must implement NIST FIPS-validated cryptography for
# the following: to provision digital signatures; to generate cryptographic
# hashes; and/or to protect unclassified information requiring
# confidentiality and cryptographic protection.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000514-AU-002890
group:           V-206510
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
cci:             CCI-002450
control_rev5:    SC-13

contribution:    Splunk can be placed in FIPS mode through splunk-launch.conf so that its
                 digital signature, hashing and TLS functions use only FIPS-validated
                 algorithms, which is the single switch the product exposes for this
                 requirement.

governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The FIPS 140 validated cryptographic module supplied by the host operating
                 system, which Splunk calls into and which splunk-launch.conf.spec:114-116
                 notes can itself place the instance in FIPS mode when the kernel runs in
                 FIPS mode
external:        The installation procedure, because the SPLK-CL-000390 fix text states
                 FIPS mode must be set before the initial start and otherwise requires a
                 reinstall or upgrade
external:        SPLUNK_COMMON_CRITERIA=1, which the SPLK-CL-000390 fix text sets alongside
                 SPLUNK_FIPS but which this release's splunk-launch.conf specification does
                 not document

citation:        SRG-APP-000514-AU-002890 check text; SPLK-CL-000390 check and fix text;
                 splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-127
finding:         splunk-launch.conf does not set SPLUNK_FIPS = 1, so the instance does not
                 run in FIPS mode and its digital signature, hashing and confidentiality
                 functions are not restricted to FIPS-validated algorithms.
